 return `<div class="sr-reading-head"><div><p class="sr-kicker">Girder span ${c.G} ft / ${s.spaces} spaces @ ${fmt(c.spacing)} ft</p><h2>A panel-load column returns a weight estimate</h2></div>${source('girder',g.page,`Original · PDF p. ${g.page}`)}</div><div class="sr-equation">R = wL/2 = ${fmt(c.wTotal,1)} × ${c.L} / 2 = ${fmt(c.R*1000,0)} lb = ${fmt(c.R)} kips<br>P = ${s.sides} × ${fmt(c.R)} + ${fmt(s.allowance,1)} allowance = ${fmt(c.P)} kips / interior panel point</div><p>Click a table cell to apply its listed depth to the 3D girder. Select a depth row and ASD panel-load column. The second header line shows the separate LRFD basis. ${c.gColumn===null?'The load exceeds the displayed columns.':`The next listed ASD column at or above the target is ${c.gColumn} kips.`}</p>${root.SteelPDFTables.html()}${status(defined&&loadOK,!defined?'This source entry is blank. It gives no weight estimate for the selected combination.':`${s.girderDepth} in / ${s.girderLoad} kip column → ${c.gWeight} plf estimated girder weight. ${loadOK?'The selected panel-load column covers the stated target.':'The selected panel-load column is below the stated target; read a higher column.'}`)}<p class="sr-small">${source('girder',1,'Read the weight-table notes')}. ${defined?`${s.girderDepth}G${s.spaces}N${s.girderLoad}K records depth, joist spaces and ASD load per interior panel point, including the stated self-weight allowance. K here means kips (1 kip = 1,000 lb), not K-series joists. N counts joist spaces, not diagonal members. ${c.gWeight<150?'7½':'10'} in minimum seat depth is anticipated by the source weight category.`:''} This is a preliminary weight lookup, not a girder capacity or deflection verification.</p>${!c.joistOK?'<p class="sr-correction">The current joist trial still needs a load check. Its reaction is shown so you can follow the arithmetic; do not treat the downstream girder as an approved selection.</p>':''}`;
